### Local environment / secrets ###
# Never commit local config or secrets. Use `.env.example` as the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docker-compose.override.yml

### Internal working notes (never committed)
/internal/

### Content ported out of a player's own cartridge (never committed)
# mmo/mods/imports tracks a recipe; `make -C mmo import` fills these from an
# image the player supplies. A second such package needs its own two lines here
# rather than a wildcard, so its bytes show up in `git status` until someone
# has decided they are ignorable.
/mmo/mods/imports/narc/
/mmo/mods/imports/port.log

# The composed sound packages: one per soundtrack/soundfont pair
# (sound_<tracks>_<font>, slugs pt/hg/bw), each tracking only its mod.toml.
# `make -C mmo soundtrack` fills replace/ and the two manifests from the
# player's own images (tools/soundtrack.py, tools/soundfont.py; the rows in
# SOUNDTRACKS and SOUNDFONTS). One family, one tool, so one pattern set
# instead of the usual per-package lines.
/mmo/mods/sound_*_*/replace/
/mmo/mods/sound_*_*/replaced.txt
/mmo/mods/sound_*_*/music.txt

# The operator's feed signing key. It signs every update players fetch;
# it never enters the repository.
feed_private.pem
*feed_private*.pem

### Stray decomp checkouts (never committed)
# Upstream trees cloned directly under decomp/, which is where
# mmo/tools/decomp_dir.sh looks when DECOMP_DIR is unset. They are listed
# rather than wildcarded so a new one shows up in `git status` until
# someone decides it is ignorable.
/decomp/pokeemerald/
/decomp/pokefirered/
/decomp/pokeheartgold/
/decomp/pokeplatinum/
